{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they made.</b> The starting point of the Tabernacle." "<b>Techelet-twisted.</b> In the language of Ishmael, weaving. Know that the grammar of cardinal numbers is different from the way of the sacred tongue, and likewise in Aramaic it is different, and also in the language of Ishmael, for always the he at the end of nouns is a sign for feminine, and masculine has no sign. But in counting three, he is a sign for masculines, and likewise in counting four, also eight, also ten. And from there onward up to twenty, the masculine has no he: אחד עשר, שנים עשר, תשעה עשר, and the feminine has he, except for the inflection of the word עשרה so that it not be confounded with masculine; they said שתים עֶשְׂרֵה and likewise all of them. And the feminine is שלש, ארבע, עשר. And if a numeral word is in construct state, it has a tav for masculines and for feminines alike: שלשת האנשים האלה (Ezekiel 14:16) and שלשת נשי בניו (Genesis 7:13). And שמונָה for masculines as is the rule, and inflected for feminine to say שמונֶה, in the manner of עשתי עשרה."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:49.427618449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}